<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">League of Armed Neutrality</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1780–1801</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The League of Armed Neutrality was an alliance of neutral naval powers formed to protect their shipping from British searches in wartime. The first league, organised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1780 with Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and later joined by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> and others, lasted until 1783. A second league of 1800 collapsed after the British victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a> in 1801.</p></div>
